  "changes": [
    "Saved 20 concise performance instructions and referenced skills/performance.md from AGENTS.md.",
    "Sparse resource and stone deposit indexes consume tile edits; placement occupancy is shared by docks and resource roads.",
    "Terrain repainting tracks disjoint dirty regions; territory retains per-source claim footprints.",
    "Separate bounded sight journals prevent crop/road appearance changes from invalidating distant fog and territory caches.",
    "Recurring and decision deadlines retain stable phases; accumulated elapsed time is preserved.",
    "Automatic city development rotates resumable city jobs: four ordinary validations, or one farm-relocation preflight, or one action per turn.",
    "Housing accrual survives queued work and saves; delayed purchases recheck permissions and live conditions.",
    "City economic storage reconciles current scalar inputs and reuses unchanged aggregates; redundant yield reads were removed and automatic relocation publishes derived rates in a later turn.",
    "Builder dispatch uses one native multi-source/multi-goal weighted search; exact minimum travel cost is preserved.",
    "Resource routing retains one active search cursor per state, bounded to 1,024 heap pops and 64 network checks per turn, with live corridor validation before dispatch.",
    "Road previews retain live filtered membership, reuse read-only context queries, and omit unused private commit tokens. Pointer feedback updates build status without refreshing the full HUD.",
    "Infantry member routes share the global movement request budget.",
    "Seven maintenance keys use 2 Hz: builders:staff,collectors:staff,farms:sync,wall-ownership,fog-raids,faction-strategies,dead-entities. Other maintenance, tactical decisions and UI retain 3 Hz; movement and hit execution remain on the fast loop."
